# What a run leaves behind splits in two, and only one half belongs in git.
#
# COMMITTED: the record -- run.json (the pins: model sha, judge version,
# dataset version, cap), events.jsonl (every attempt, verdict and tool call),
# clusters.jsonl and diagnoses.jsonl, the model snapshot, and the write-up.
# Together they are what makes a past number re-readable. Twenty-two runs of
# another set kept 40MB of transcripts and lost every run.json, so the scores
# survived with nothing saying what produced them.
#
# IGNORED: the bulk and the derived. artifacts/ is the per-case transcripts and
# judge replies -- 2.7MB of a 3.1MB run, re-readable from events.jsonl for the
# parts that matter. A built report package is derived from the record by
# build_run_package.py, and worse, it is a Malloy package: nested inside
# examples/storefront its eval_run.malloy resolves duckdb.table('data/*.csv')
# against the STOREFRONT package root, which puts storefront itself into
# loadErrors and it serves nothing. Build it into /tmp.
*/runs/*/artifacts/
*/runs/**/run-package-*/
run-package-*/
